      "description": "Get to know the Thales FMS 220 of the ATR 42/72, one key at a time.\n\nThis simulator reproduces the MCDU of the FMS 220: the screen layout, the colours, the line select keys, the scratchpad and the page logic. Use it to practise at home, on the crew bus or during a hotel night, so you arrive at the simulator or the aircraft already knowing the workflow.\n\nFLIGHT PLANNING\n• FPLN INIT: origin, destination, flight ID, cruise level and stored pilot routes\n• Departures, arrivals and runways from the built-in navigation database\n• Airway entry, next waypoint, new destination and secondary flight plan\n• Lateral revisions: DIRECT TO, DTO ABEAM, holding patterns, offsets and overfly\n• Vertical revisions: altitude and speed constraints, RTA, step climbs and winds\n\nPERFORMANCE AND PREDICTIONS\n• PERF INIT with weights, reserves, cruise mode and fuel flow factor\n• Takeoff and approach speeds (VmHB, VAPP) computed from representative performance tables\n• Climb, cruise, holding and descent predictions in normal and icing conditions\n• ETA, distance and estimated fuel on board for every waypoint, top of descent and destination\n• One engine out ceilings\n\nNAVIGATION\n• Position initialisation and sensor status\n• Progress page with VNAV information\n• Nearest airports and navaids, bearing/distance and place/bearing/distance data\n\nDATA AND RADIOS\n• Browse the standard database: airports, waypoints, navaids, NDBs and runways\n• Create and store your own pilot waypoints, navaids, airports and routes\n• Radio management pages for navigation, communication and transponder\n\nSIMULATOR OPTIONS\n• Set the temperature deviation (ΔISA) and icing conditions\n• Choose the descent speed\n• Adjust FMS and input lag to match the feel of the real unit, or turn them off\n\nRuns on iPhone, iPad, Mac and Apple Vision Pro. Works fully offline. One-time purchase, no subscription.\n\nFOR TRAINING ONLY\nThis app is a simulation for familiarisation and training. It is not certified, not approved by any aviation authority and must never be used for real flight planning or navigation. The navigation database is a fixed simulation dataset that does not represent the real world, and performance predictions are simplified.\n\nThis app is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by ATR or Thales.\n\nQuestions or suggestions? Use MCDU MENU > FEEDBACK inside the app.",
